  "editorialSummary": "Nothing captures our delicate societal architecture quite like global markets reeling from a [Binance crypto heist](https://arstechnica.com/information-technology/2026/11/dacynsays-hackers-who-stole-billions-in-crypto-spent-months-planning-heist) while hackers also [cripple French blood banks](https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-11-05/french-blood-banks-hit-alongside-cyberattack-on-european-superma/107348302) and lawmakers grapple with [a Democratic congressional rout](https://www.dw.com/en/democrats-take-house-and-senate-from-republicans-in-us-midterm-rout/a-79859416?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-rdf). Fortunately, paleontologists have managed to recover [fossilised dinosaur red blood cells](https://www.theguardian.com/science/2026/nov/02/fossilised-red-blood-cells-aratasaurus-dinosaurs-bone) from an ancient bone, giving future archaeologists something sturdy to examine once we finish rendering ourselves entirely extinct.",
